{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979287675,"sessionID":"ses_1cc928c72ffem1Hk8Ljv6sTaPj","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_JHbkldhVp3a0Qa7Zxem973dd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"Hi!  My suggestion is to change the term name to \\\"chronic myeloid leukemia\\\" as it is the preferred and most common name, with \\\"Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia\\\" being an older synonym;   I understand that the full name \\\"Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia, BCR-ABL1 positive\\\" is more precise because CML is defined by the presence of the BCR-ABL1 gene, distinguishing it from rare CML-like disorders, and should be kept as a synonym. \\n\\nChronic myeloid leukemia is the standard term used by the National Cancer Institute, and National Institutes of Health, and major health organizations like the American Cancer Society,\\nPlease see: \\nhttps://www.cancer.gov/types/leukemia/patient/cml-treatment-pdq\\nhttps://medlineplus.gov/genetics/condition/chronic-myeloid-leukemia/#synonyms\\nhttps://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/chronic-myeloid-leukemia/about/what-is-cml.html\\n\\nThank you,  Gioconda Alyea\\n\\n\",\n3:   \"comments\": [],\n4:   \"title\": \"chronic myelogenous leukemia, BCR-ABL1 positive\",\n5:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9892\"\n6: }\n\n(End of file - total 6 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"Hi!  My suggestion is to change the term name to \\\"chronic myeloid leukemia\\\" as it is the preferred and most common name, with \\\"Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia\\\" being an older synonym;   I understand that the full name \\\"Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia, BCR-ABL1 positive\\\" is more precise because CML is defined by the presence of the BCR-ABL1 gene, distinguishing it from rare CML-like disorders, and should be kept as a synonym. \\n\\nChronic myeloid leukemia is the standard term used by the National Cancer Institute, and National Institutes of Health, and major health organizations like the American Cancer Society,\\nPlease see: \\nhttps://www.cancer.gov/types/leukemia/patient/cml-treatment-pdq\\nhttps://medlineplus.gov/genetics/condition/chronic-myeloid-leukemia/#synonyms\\nhttps://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/chronic-myeloid-leukemia/about/what-is-cml.html\\n\\nThank you,  Gioconda Alyea\\n\\n\",\n  \"comments\": [],\n  \"title\": \"chronic myelogenous leukemia, BCR-ABL1 positive\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9892\"\n}","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"__issue_context__.json","time":{"start":1778979287660,"end":1778979287672}},"id":"prt_e336db2630017Q3cxzR3kpBT1p","sessionID":"ses_1cc928c72ffem1Hk8Ljv6sTaPj","messageID":"msg_e336da0f5001PBEuHn36zGuV3M"}}
